{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788294237,"nonce":"W4jVLW8bLFpBd261xyX22d1KBcg=","message":"THE BENCH RUN THIS SPEC WAS WAITING FOR. Comment #10 ended \"No verb was run against a bench; everything above is static verification\". It has now been run: `accept/3.5-dialog-verbs.py` against `_RimWorld-Agent` session `20260901T195344`, assembly `1.0.0+094b14a`.\n\n**226 checks, 0 failed, 0 skipped, exit 0** — read directly from `$?`, never through a pipe. Log and the full run sequence: `accept/runs/s20-20260901/` (`3.5-full5.log` is the recorded one; the eight earlier logs are kept because the sequence is the evidence).\n\n## Zero mod defects. Eight driver defects, and one of them refutes this issue's own close condition\n\nThe \"Minimum to close\" in comment #8 was **`7e8c969`'s `data.after` fix, then one re-run**. That premise does not survive the run. `data.after` is CORRECT and there is nothing to fix in it — see the comment I have just left on `7e8c969`.\n\n3.9g and 3.9h asserted that a bought good is colony stock the moment the deal executes. It is not:\n\n- `RimWorld/Tradeable.ResolveTrade` hands a buy to `TransferableUtility.TransferNoSplit(thingsTrader, …)`, which walks the trader's stack LIST and calls `RimWorld/Pawn_TraderTracker.GiveSoldThingToPlayer` **once per stack**.\n- That method places each with `GenPlace.TryPlaceThing(thing, toGive.PositionHeld, mapHeld, ThingPlaceMode.Near)` — at **whichever caravan member was carrying it**, not near the negotiator.\n- The rebuilt deal's colony-side count is `ColonyThingsWillingToBuy`, whose test is `Home[pos] || IsInAnyStorage()` plus unfogged and reachable.\n\nSo bought goods are legitimately not colony stock until hauled, and vanilla's own `Dialog_Trade` prints the same optimistic post-deal column. Three consecutive live deals, all correct and all different: paying 360 moved the colony count by exactly **-360**; receiving 83 moved it by **0**; receiving 80 moved it by **69**. An outflow is exact — the stacks are taken FROM colony scope. An inflow is a fraction: however many carriers happened to stand inside the home area.\n\nThe suite now asserts equality on the outflow, a BOUND on the inflow, and proves delivery on the two numbers that are not deal-scoped — the trader's own holdings (972 -\u003e 889 and 103 -\u003e 93, exact both times) and an independent whole-map `things {def}` read.\n\n## The other seven, all driver-side, all found only by running it\n\n- **A `precondition` skip left a trade session open.** `precondition()` calls `sys.exit(2)` and phase 3 has five of them after `trade-start`. The NEXT run's phase 0 then failed 0.8a / 0.8b / 0.11 — three red checks with nothing to do with the mod. `send()` now tracks the session and an `atexit` hook closes it however the process leaves.\n- **The fixture took `traders[0]` and assumed willingness.** `CanTradeNow` is per-trader; a departing caravan and an arriving one coexisted on the map and the arriving one sorted first, so a run skipped at 3.2pre with a perfectly willing trader standing there. It now opens sessions until one takes, which is what a player does.\n- **3.4d's guidance named a \"trade radius\" that does not exist**, and it cost a staging round: 2000 silver spawned ON the trader's own cell counted as ZERO, the same 2000 at the negotiator counted in full.\n- **An unpowered comms console presented as eight red checks** in 5.3/5.6 rather than a fixture skip. A solar generator staged at 16:00 stops generating at sunset, so a suite green at 16:00 goes red at 22:00 with nothing about the mod having changed. Now a named precondition (5.1p) that says which and tells you to advance to daylight.\n- Plus the three phase-0 checks that the leaked session was failing.\n\n## Acceptance, against the body's three bullets\n\n1. **\"buy 10 meals + sell 5 shirts sight-unseen via verbs; silver and stock verified correct after confirm; cancel leaves state untouched\"** — met. Buy and sell in ONE `trade-set` call on distinct defs, `lines_with_action == 3`, the trader's holdings verified exactly on both lines, the currency line verified against the deal's own promise, and 3.7i/3.7j/3.7k prove cancel left colony silver, trader stock and colony stock all unchanged. Zero force-pausing windows across the whole phase.\n2. **\"Choice letter (quest offer) accepted via verb -\u003e quest active\"** — met, phase 2, including the red-error trap: an accept with a choice outstanding is REFUSED and cites the widget clause, and 2.3g asserts the refusal logged no red error.\n3. **\"A modded/unknown dialog shows opaque in interactions and dismisses cleanly\"** — met, phase 4, plus amendment #2's real requirement: the run is UN-WEDGED afterwards.\n\nThe one thing still NOT proven here, and it is the orchestrator's by construction: **1.2c, the byte-identical-save half of bullet 4.** The script cannot save without perturbing the counters it is checking. It is a NOTE in the log, not a silent omission.\n\n## Fixture, recorded so the next runner does not pay for it again\n\n`--quicktest`, then `dev:spawn-thing` Silver / ComponentIndustrial / MealSurvivalPack at `pos:\"pawn:\u003cnegotiator\u003e\"` (the HOME AREA is the test, not distance to the trader) · `dev:spawn-thing CommsConsole` + `SolarGenerator` within 6 cells (`RimWorld/PowerConnectionMaker.ConnectMaxDist = 6`) and one advance so the power net forms · `dev:incident GiveQuest_Random` until `quests.counts.available \u003e= 1` · run in daylight.\n\nCommit `32735d4`.","files":null}]}